1
00:00:01,820 --> 00:00:23,360
A Real Stewart

2
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:26,730
There's nothing more joyous than the arrival of a new baby.

3
00:00:26,730 --> 00:00:28,700
I am so excited. Mother!

4
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:31,930
Just imagine--Marilyn and Richard must be thrilled!

5
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:34,090
Oh, a new baby!

6
00:00:34,090 --> 00:00:38,780
Max ... Max ... Max.

7
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:44,120
Oh, it's a sweet-sounding name for a sweet little boy.

8
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:47,230
My first grandchild.

9
00:00:47,230 --> 00:00:50,220
And my first nephew.

10
00:00:50,220 --> 00:00:52,930
Isn't he just adorable?

11
00:00:52,930 --> 00:00:55,710
He looks a lot like you, Mom. He does.

12
00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:59,160
Do you think so?

13
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:02,080
Well, I guess. He does look a lot like Richard,

14
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:05,940
and I guess he looks a lot like me.

15
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:09,040
Oh, he's got Richard's eyes, though.

16
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:13,110
I really want Harry and Michelle to see Max.

17
00:01:13,110 --> 00:01:14,140
When are they coming?

18
00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:17,720
Tomorrow. Harry has an account to work on today.

19
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:22,110
Yes, he does have Richard's eyes. Big blue eyes.

20
00:01:22,110 --> 00:01:24,340
[01:20.17]The baby even looks at you like Richard does.

21
00:01:24,340 --> 00:01:27,010
Well, children usually resemble their parents.

22
00:01:27,010 --> 00:01:28,620
It's true.

23
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:31,660
Michelle is a lot like Harry in so many ways.

24
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:36,270
And she's shy with new people, just like he is.

25
00:01:36,270 --> 00:01:39,210
You really like Michelle, don't you?

26
00:01:39,210 --> 00:01:41,960
Yes. I'm very fond of her.

27
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:46,430
And Harry, too?

28
00:01:46,430 --> 00:01:47,470
Well ...

29
00:01:47,470 --> 00:01:50,380
Uh, it's four-thirty. Oh my!

30
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:52,830
Marilyn and Richard will be home from the hospital any minute,

31
00:01:52,830 --> 00:01:55,480
and we must prepare this room.

32
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:58,300
Where will we put all the presents?

33
00:01:58,300 --> 00:02:01,180
Well, let's take everything to the living room.

34
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:04,540
Marilyn and Richard and the baby need the space.

35
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:08,120
It's crowded in here.

36
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:10,050
The welcome sign is up:

37
00:02:10,050 --> 00:02:11,730
"Welcome home, Max."

38
00:02:11,730 --> 00:02:14,280
Isn't it exciting, Grandpa?

39
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:17,260
Your first great-grandchild.

40
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:21,110
Yes. Yes, sir.

41
00:02:21,110 --> 00:02:25,470
A great-grandchild. A great-grandson.

42
00:02:25,470 --> 00:02:29,010
Another generation to carry on the Stewart name.

43
00:02:29,010 --> 00:02:30,620
I love you, Grandpa.

44
00:02:30,620 --> 00:02:35,130
You make me feel so proud to be part of our family.

45
00:02:35,130 --> 00:02:37,570
One day, you'll have your own family,

46
00:02:37,570 --> 00:02:41,020
and I'll be proud to be part of it.

47
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:44,010
Now you understand my feelings, Susan.

48
00:02:44,010 --> 00:02:48,280
I'm Grandpa's daughter-in-law, but I feel like a Stewart.

49
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:51,300
He's always made me feel like his own daughter.

50
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:52,210
Well,

51
00:02:52,210 --> 00:02:58,950
that's because you're so much like us--wonderful!

52
00:02:58,950 --> 00:03:05,020
Mom, got it.

53
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:07,760
This will make a nice gift for Marilyn and Richard.

54
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:10,000
They can keep a record of all of the important dates

55
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,830
and information about Max's life here.

56
00:03:12,830 --> 00:03:14,700
Let's see.

57
00:03:14,700 --> 00:03:18,160
Name: Max Stewart.

58
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:20,100
Does he have a middle name?

59
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:24,200
No, just Max. I like that.

60
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:26,720
No middle name. No middle initial.

61
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:30,500
Like me. I'm Malcolm Stewart.

62
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:33,200
Just Malcolm Stewart.

63
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:35,170
And Max has your initials, Grandpa:

64
00:03:35,170 --> 00:03:42,700
Uh, it must mean something.

65
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:46,160
Weight: eight pounds six ounces.

66
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:49,880
Eight-six. Big boy!

67
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:52,050
All the Stewart men were big.

68
00:03:52,050 --> 00:03:55,050
Well, Robbie was eight pounds two ounces,

69
00:03:55,050 --> 00:03:57,740
and Richard was eight pounds three.

70
00:03:57,740 --> 00:03:59,910
And me?

71
00:03:59,910 --> 00:04:02,580
Eight pounds six.

72
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:06,090
You were big, just like Max.

73
00:04:06,090 --> 00:04:08,300
Eight pounds six, just like me.

74
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:11,750
That's nice. Length. Length?

75
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:15,600
Richard says Max is twenty-one inches long.

76
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:18,520
Twenty-one inches.

77
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:21,280
Is that tall or average or what?

78
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:26,010
Tall. All the Stewart men are tall.

79
00:04:26,010 --> 00:04:31,840
Well, Grandpa, you're about five-nine or five-ten.

80
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:35,350
I wouldn't call that tall.

81
00:04:35,350 --> 00:04:37,450
I take after my mother's family.

82
00:04:37,450 --> 00:04:43,140
They were ... they were ... they were average.

83
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:50,890
Mother: Marilyn. Father: Richard.

84
00:04:50,890 --> 00:04:56,240
And lots of pages for Richard's photos of Max.

85
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:59,440
Speaking of mother and of father

86
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:02,690
--and speaking of Max--I hear the car.

87
00:05:02,690 --> 00:05:03,770
They're here!

88
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:08,940
Oh! Oh, quickly! Go, go, go!

89
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:12,300
Let's see. Oh, welcome home.

90
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:13,120
Oh, let her in.

91
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:14,500
Wait with your pictures for a second.

92
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:17,100
Come on, darlings.

93
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:21,790
Sweetheart .... Sit down right here.

94
00:05:21,790 --> 00:05:26,680
Oh, he's so cute! Oh, Marilyn!

95
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:29,040
Max looks just like Grandpa.

96
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:30,940
A real Stewart.

97
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:33,940
I'm so happy to be home with my family--and with Max.
